-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_41.sql (Isaiah 41) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 41 — FEAR NOT / THE IDOLS ARE NOTHING. The covenant-lawsuit court is convened:
-- *Keep silence before me, O islands... let us come near together to judgment* (41:1). Yahuah names
-- the One He raised up *from the east* (41:2 = Abraham, the called seed), then turns to the people
-- HE chose: *But thou, Yashar'el (Israel), art my servant, Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of
-- Abraham my friend* (41:8) — *I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away* (41:9), the two-house
-- election guard against any casting-off. Then the great FEAR NOT: *Fear thou not; for I am with
-- thee... I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness* (41:10); *For I Yahuah Elohayka
-- (the LORD thy God) will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee* (41:13);
-- *thy redeemer, the Holy One of Yashar'el (Israel)* (41:14). LIVING WATER for the thirsty: *I will
-- open rivers in high places... I will make the wilderness a pool of water* (41:18). And the verdict
-- on the gods of the nations: *Behold, ye are of nothing, and your work of nought* (41:24); *Behold,
-- they are all vanity; their works are nothing: their molten images are wind and confusion* (41:29) —
-- because Yahuah ALONE foretells: *Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know?* (41:26).
-- The court of the idols collapses; the One who calls the generations from the beginning (41:4) holds
-- His servant by the right hand. Conduct and covenant, never ethnic; the servant is upheld, not cast off.
-- Tag: isa41   Temp view: _s303_isa41_lookup
-- Sort band: base 27000, step 3 -> threads at 27000, 27003, 27006, 27009 (4 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',41,v
--
-- Isaiah 41 coverage:
--   v.2,8-9 (Who raised up the righteous man from the east... But thou, Yashar'el, art my servant,
--          Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of Abraham my friend... I have chosen thee, and not cast
--          thee away)
--        NT:     ★ James 2:23 (Abraham believed Elohim... and he was called the Friend of Elohim),
--                Romans 4:11-12 (the father of all them that believe... who also walk in the steps of
--                that faith of our father Abraham) — THREAD 1
--        Extras: none warranted (the friend-of-Elohim title is carried clean by James; no extra forced)
--        Tanakh: ★ Genesis 12:1 (Get thee out of thy country... unto a land that I will shew thee) —
--                THREAD 1 (the calling of the seed from the east)
--   ★★ v.10,13-14 (Fear thou not; for I am with thee... I will uphold thee with the right hand of my
--          righteousness... For I Yahuah Elohayka will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not;
--          I will help thee... thy redeemer, the Holy One of Yashar'el)
--        NT:     ★★ Hebrews 13:5-6 (I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee... I will not fear what
--                man shall do unto me), ★ Matthew 28:20 (lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of
--                the world) — THREAD 2
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★★ Isaiah 43:1-2,5 (Fear not... I will be with thee... Fear not: for I am with thee),
--                ★ Deuteronomy 31:6,8 (he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee... fear not, neither be
--                dismayed) — THREAD 2 (the great Fear-Not, woven across the prophets and the Torah)
--   v.17-18 (When the poor and needy seek water, and there is none... I Yahuah will hear them... I
--          will open rivers in high places... I will make the wilderness a pool of water)
--        NT:     ★ John 7:37-38 (If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink... out of his belly
--                shall flow rivers of living water) — THREAD 3
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 35:6-7 (in the wilderness shall waters break out, and streams in the desert),
--                ★ Isaiah 44:3 (I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry
--                ground) — THREAD 3 (living water for the thirsty; the Spirit poured)
--   ★ v.24,29 (Behold, ye are of nothing, and your work of nought... Behold, they are all vanity;
--          their works are nothing: their molten images are wind and confusion); v.26 (Who hath
--          declared from the beginning? — Yahuah alone foretells)
--        NT:     ★ 1 Corinthians 8:4 (an idol is nothing in the world, and there is none other Elohim
--                but one) — THREAD 4
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Psalm 115:4-8 (Their idols are silver and gold... they have mouths, but they speak
--                not), ★ Jeremiah 10:14-15 (every founder is confounded by the graven image... they are
--                vanity, and the work of errors), Isaiah 46:9-10 (Declaring the end from the beginning
--                — lateral on 41:26, the One who alone foretells) — THREAD 4 (the idols are nothing)
--   v.1 (the court convened), v.3-7 (the nations' fear / the carpenter encourageth the goldsmith —
--          the idol-making woven into THREAD 4 in prose), v.4 (I Yahuah, the first... I am he — woven
--          into THREAD 4), v.11-12 (they shall be as nothing — woven into THREAD 2's enemies), v.15-16
--          (the threshing instrument — held in prose), v.19-23 (the planting / produce your cause —
--          the court-challenge woven into THREAD 4), v.25,27-28 (one from the north / no counsellor —
--          woven into THREAD 4). All weighed; none silently skipped.
--
-- Threads (slug — target libraries):
--   1. isaiah-41-abraham-my-friend-the-called-seed — NT (James 2, Romans 4) + Tanakh (Genesis 12) [free]
--      (Abraham my friend, the seed called from the east; chosen and not cast away)
--   2. isaiah-41-fear-thou-not-for-i-am-with-thee — NT (Hebrews 13, Matthew 28) + Tanakh (Isaiah 43,
--      Deuteronomy 31) [free] (★★ the great Fear-Not; the right hand that upholds, never forsakes)
--   3. isaiah-41-rivers-in-high-places-for-the-thirsty — NT (John 7) + Tanakh (Isaiah 35, Isaiah 44)
--      [free] (living water for the poor and needy; the Spirit poured on the dry ground)
--   4. isaiah-41-the-idols-are-nothing-wind-and-confusion — NT (1 Corinthians 8) + Tanakh (Psalm 115,
--      Jeremiah 10) [free] (★ the gods of the nations are nothing; Yahuah alone foretells)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ABRAHAM MY FRIEND (THREAD 1): the One *raised up... from the east, called... to his foot* (41:2) is
--      Abraham, and the people are *the seed of Abraham my friend* (41:8). The calling is Genesis 12:1
--      (*Get thee out of thy country... unto a land that I will shew thee*); the title is James 2:23
--      (*he was called the Friend of Elohim*) — and that friendship was faith made perfect by works
--      (James 2:22), carried by paternal bloodline AND covenant-word, the seed who *walk in the steps
--      of that faith* (Romans 4:12). *I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away* (41:9) is the
--      election-guard: Yahuah does not cast off the seed He called.
--   ★★ THE GREAT FEAR-NOT (THREAD 2): *Fear thou not; for I am with thee... I will uphold thee with the
--      right hand of my righteousness* (41:10); *I Yahuah Elohayka will hold thy right hand, saying...
--      Fear not; I will help thee* (41:13). This is one promise sung across the whole library: the
--      Torah-word to Yashar'el (*he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee... fear not, neither be
--      dismayed*, Deuteronomy 31:6,8), the prophet's echo (*Fear not... I will be with thee... Fear
--      not: for I am with thee*, Isaiah 43:1-2,5), the apostolic word (*I will never leave thee, nor
--      forsake thee*, Hebrews 13:5-6), and the Formed Son's own closing word (*lo, I am with you alway*,
--      Matthew 28:20). The redeemer who holds the right hand is *the Holy One of Yashar'el* (41:14).
--   LIVING WATER (THREAD 3): *When the poor and needy seek water, and there is none... I Yahuah will
--      hear them... I will open rivers in high places... I will make the wilderness a pool of water*
--      (41:17-18). The same promise blossoms in Isaiah 35:6-7 (*in the wilderness shall waters break
--      out*) and Isaiah 44:3 (*I will pour water upon him that is thirsty... I will pour my spirit upon
--      thy seed*) — water and Spirit together. The Formed Son fills it at the feast of tabernacles:
--      *If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink... out of his belly shall flow rivers of
--      living water* (John 7:37-38).
--   ★ THE IDOLS ARE NOTHING (THREAD 4): the court verdict on the gods of the nations — *Behold, ye are
--      of nothing, and your work of nought* (41:24); *they are all vanity; their works are nothing:
--      their molten images are wind and confusion* (41:29). The whole library says the same: *Their
--      idols are silver and gold... they have mouths, but they speak not* (Psalm 115:4-5); *every
--      founder is confounded by the graven image... they are vanity, and the work of errors* (Jeremiah
--      10:14-15); *an idol is nothing in the world, and there is none other Elohim but one* (1
--      Corinthians 8:4). The reason the idols are nothing is sealed in 41:26 — only Yahuah *declares
--      from the beginning* (lateral Isaiah 46:9-10, *Declaring the end from the beginning*).
--   VERSES WITH NO SEPARATE ADD: v.1 (the court convened — preface to THREAD 4), v.3-7 (the nations'
--      fear and the idol-makers encouraging one another — woven into THREAD 4's prose), v.11-12 (the
--      enemies as nothing — woven into THREAD 2), v.15-16 (the threshing instrument), v.19-23 (the
--      planting and the court-challenge), v.25,27-28 (one from the north, no counsellor). All recorded.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa41_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1: Abraham my friend — the seed called from the east
    ('canon','isaiah',41,8,'canon','genesis',12,1,'free',
      E'*Now Yahuah (LORD) had said unto Abram, Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father''s house, unto a land that I will shew thee* (Genesis 12:1). The One *raised up... from the east* (Isaiah 41:2) and named *the seed of Abraham my friend* (Isaiah 41:8) is the called Abraham — called out of his country to the land Yahuah would shew him. The servant-people are that called seed; the friendship begins with the calling-word, *Get thee out... unto a land that I will shew thee*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,8,'canon','james',2,23,'free',
      E'*And the scripture was fulfilled which saith, Abraham believed Elohim (God), and it was imputed unto him for righteousness: and he was called the Friend of Elohim (God)* (James 2:23). Isaiah names the people *the seed of Abraham my friend* (Isaiah 41:8); James names where the title comes from — Abraham *was called the Friend of Elohim*, a friendship that was *faith made perfect* by works (2:22), believing-word and obedient-walk together. The servant-people inherit the friend''s name and the friend''s faith.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,8,'canon','romans',4,11,'free',
      E'*And he received the sign of circumcision, a seal of the righteousness of the faith which he had yet being uncircumcised: that he might be the father of all them that believe* (Romans 4:11). *The seed of Abraham my friend* (Isaiah 41:8) is the called seed of the father of the faithful — the seed who *walk in the steps of that faith of our father Abraham* (Romans 4:12). The election is by paternal bloodline AND the believing-walk together, never lineage alone, never confession alone.'),

    -- THREAD 2 (★★): Fear thou not, for I am with thee — the right hand that upholds
    ('canon','isaiah',41,10,'canon','isaiah',43,2,'free',
      E'*When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee* (Isaiah 43:2). The *Fear thou not; for I am with thee* of Isaiah 41:10 is unfolded in the next great Fear-Not: *Fear not... I will be with thee* (43:1-2). The same presence that upholds *with the right hand of my righteousness* (41:10) walks the servant through the waters and the fire unharmed.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,13,'canon','isaiah',43,5,'free',
      E'*Fear not: for I am with thee: I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west* (Isaiah 43:5). *For I Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee* (Isaiah 41:13) — and the Fear-Not is the same word that gathers the scattered seed home from every direction (43:5). The hand that holds the servant''s right hand is the hand that regathers the two-house people.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,13,'canon','deuteronomy',31,8,'free',
      E'*And Yahuah (LORD), he it is that doth go before thee; he will be with thee, he will not fail thee, neither forsake thee: fear not, neither be dismayed* (Deuteronomy 31:8). The *Fear not; I will help thee* of Isaiah 41:13 is the Torah''s own word to Yashar''el (Israel): *Be strong and of a good courage, fear not... he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee* (Deuteronomy 31:6). The covenant promise stands from Moses to the prophet unchanged — *he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,10,'canon','hebrews',13,5,'free',
      E'*Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee* (Hebrews 13:5). The *I am with thee... I will uphold thee* of Isaiah 41:10 is the apostolic ground of fearlessness: *he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee*. The same covenant word Moses spoke (Deuteronomy 31) is the believer''s anchor against fear.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,10,'canon','hebrews',13,6,'free',
      E'*So that we may boldly say, Yahuah (Lord) is my helper, and I will not fear what man shall do unto me* (Hebrews 13:6). Because Yahuah says *Fear thou not; for I am with thee... I will help thee* (Isaiah 41:10), the servant may *boldly say, Yahuah (Lord) is my helper, and I will not fear what man shall do unto me*. The helping hand of righteousness silences the fear of man — *all they that were incensed against thee shall be ashamed* (41:11).'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,10,'canon','matthew',28,20,'free',
      E'*Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world. Amen* (Matthew 28:20). The *I am with thee* of Isaiah 41:10 is the Formed Son''s own closing word — *lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world*. The presence that upheld the servant with *the right hand of my righteousness* is the abiding presence to the end of the age.'),

    -- THREAD 3: Rivers in high places — living water for the thirsty
    ('canon','isaiah',41,17,'canon','john',7,37,'free',
      E'*In the last day, that great day of the feast, Yahusha (Jesus) stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink* (John 7:37). When *the poor and needy seek water, and there is none, and their tongue faileth for thirst, I Yahuah (LORD) will hear them* (Isaiah 41:17) — and the Formed Son answers the thirst at the feast of tabernacles: *If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink*. The One who opens the rivers IS the One who gives the living water.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,18,'canon','john',7,38,'free',
      E'*He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water* (John 7:38). *I will open rivers in high places... I will make the wilderness a pool of water* (Isaiah 41:18) is fulfilled when *out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water* — the Spirit poured (7:39). The rivers in the high places and the rivers from within the believer are one outpouring.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,18,'canon','isaiah',35,6,'free',
      E'*Then shall the lame man leap as an hart, and the tongue of the dumb sing: for in the wilderness shall waters break out, and streams in the desert* (Isaiah 35:6). *I will open rivers in high places... I will make the wilderness a pool of water* (Isaiah 41:18) is the same desert turned to springs: *in the wilderness shall waters break out, and streams in the desert*. The thirsty land of 41:17 becomes *a pool, and the thirsty land springs of water* (35:7).'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,18,'canon','isaiah',44,3,'free',
      E'*For I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry ground: I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thine offspring* (Isaiah 44:3). The rivers and pools of Isaiah 41:18 are named as the Spirit poured: *I will pour water upon him that is thirsty... I will pour my spirit upon thy seed*. Water and Ruach are one gift on the dry ground of the needy seed.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★): The idols are nothing — wind and confusion; Yahuah alone foretells
    ('canon','isaiah',41,24,'canon','1-corinthians',8,4,'free',
      E'*As concerning therefore the eating of those things that are offered in sacrifice unto idols, we know that an idol is nothing in the world, and that there is none other Elohim (God) but one* (1 Corinthians 8:4). The court verdict *Behold, ye are of nothing, and your work of nought* (Isaiah 41:24) is the apostle''s plain confession: *an idol is nothing in the world, and there is none other Elohim but one*. The gods of the nations have no being; only Yahuah is.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,29,'canon','psalms',115,4,'free',
      E'*Their idols are silver and gold, the work of men''s hands* (Psalm 115:4). *Their molten images are wind and confusion* (Isaiah 41:29) — and the psalm shows why: they are *silver and gold, the work of men''s hands*, that *have mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not* (115:4-5). A thing the craftsman makes cannot answer; *they that make them are like unto them* (115:8).'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,29,'canon','psalms',115,5,'free',
      E'*They have mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not* (Psalm 115:5). *They are all vanity; their works are nothing* (Isaiah 41:29) because the idol *hath mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not*. The court of 41 asked the gods to *shew the things that are to come* (41:23) — but a thing with a carved mouth that cannot speak is *wind and confusion*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,29,'canon','jeremiah',10,14,'free',
      E'*Every man is brutish in his knowledge: every founder is confounded by the graven image: for his molten image is falsehood, and there is no breath in them* (Jeremiah 10:14). *Their molten images are wind and confusion* (Isaiah 41:29) is Jeremiah''s verdict exactly: *his molten image is falsehood, and there is no breath in them*. The maker is confounded by the very thing he made; there is no breath, no being, in it.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,29,'canon','jeremiah',10,15,'free',
      E'*They are vanity, and the work of errors: in the time of their visitation they shall perish* (Jeremiah 10:15). The idols that *are all vanity; their works are nothing* (Isaiah 41:29) are Jeremiah''s *vanity, and the work of errors* — and they have an end: *in the time of their visitation they shall perish*. The gods of nought cannot stand the day of reckoning.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',41,26,'canon','isaiah',46,9,'free',
      E'*Remember the former things of old: for I am Elohim (God), and there is none else; I am Elohim (God), and there is none like me, Declaring the end from the beginning, and from ancient times the things that are not yet done* (Isaiah 46:9-10). The court of 41 asks *Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know?* (Isaiah 41:26) — and the answer is Yahuah alone, *Declaring the end from the beginning*. This is why the idols are nothing: only the One who foretells the latter end is Elohim.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa41_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa41_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-41-abraham-my-friend-the-called-seed',
       E'Abraham my friend — the seed called from the east',
       E'In the convened court Yahuah names the One He raised up to do His will: *Who raised up the righteous man from the east, called him to his foot, gave the nations before him, and made him rule over kings?* (Isaiah 41:2). Then He turns to the people He chose and binds them to that man: *But thou, Yashar''el (Israel), art my servant, Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of Abraham my friend* (41:8); *Thou whom I have taken from the ends of the earth... I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away* (41:9). The friendship began with a calling-word: *Now Yahuah (LORD) had said unto Abram, Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father''s house, unto a land that I will shew thee* (Genesis 12:1). And James names the title Isaiah leans on: *Abraham believed Elohim (God), and it was imputed unto him for righteousness: and he was called the Friend of Elohim (God)* (James 2:23) — a friendship that was *faith made perfect* by works (2:22), believing-word and obedient-walk together. The servant-people are that called seed, the seed who *walk in the steps of that faith of our father Abraham* (Romans 4:12) — election by paternal bloodline AND covenant-word, never lineage alone, never confession alone. And the great guard rings in 41:9: *I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away* — Yahuah does not cast off the seed He called His friend.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27000
  FROM _s303_isa41_lookup sv, _s303_isa41_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=41 AND sv.verse_number=8
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=41 AND ev.verse_number=9
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-41-fear-thou-not-for-i-am-with-thee',
       E'Fear thou not, for I am with thee — the right hand that upholds and never forsakes',
       E'The heart of the chapter is the great Fear-Not: *Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy Elohim (God): I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness* (Isaiah 41:10); *For I Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee* (41:13); *Fear not, thou worm Jacob, and ye men of Yashar''el (Israel); I will help thee, saith Yahuah (LORD), and thy redeemer, the Holy One of Yashar''el (Israel)* (41:14). This is one promise sung across the whole library. It is the Torah''s own word to Yashar''el: *Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee* (Deuteronomy 31:6); *he will not fail thee, neither forsake thee: fear not, neither be dismayed* (31:8). It is the prophet''s own next Fear-Not: *Fear not... When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee... Fear not: for I am with thee: I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west* (Isaiah 43:1-2,5) — the hand that holds the servant''s right hand is the hand that regathers the scattered two-house seed. It is the apostolic anchor: *he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee. So that we may boldly say, Yahuah (Lord) is my helper, and I will not fear what man shall do unto me* (Hebrews 13:5-6). And it is the Formed Son''s own closing word: *lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world* (Matthew 28:20). One promise, Torah to prophet to apostle to the Son: the right hand of righteousness upholds, and never forsakes.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27003
  FROM _s303_isa41_lookup sv, _s303_isa41_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=41 AND sv.verse_number=10
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=41 AND ev.verse_number=14
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-41-rivers-in-high-places-for-the-thirsty',
       E'Rivers in high places — living water for the poor and needy',
       E'To the parched and failing Yahuah promises water from nowhere: *When the poor and needy seek water, and there is none, and their tongue faileth for thirst, I Yahuah (LORD) will hear them, I the Elohim (God) of Yashar''el (Israel) will not forsake them. I will open rivers in high places, and fountains in the midst of the valleys: I will make the wilderness a pool of water, and the dry land springs of water* (Isaiah 41:17-18). The same wonder blossoms across Isaiah: *in the wilderness shall waters break out, and streams in the desert. And the parched ground shall become a pool, and the thirsty land springs of water* (Isaiah 35:6-7); and the water is named as the Spirit: *For I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry ground: I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thine offspring* (Isaiah 44:3) — water and Ruach one gift on the dry ground of the seed. The Formed Son fills it at the feast of tabernacles: *In the last day, that great day of the feast, Yahusha (Jesus) stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink. He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water* (John 7:37-38). The rivers Yahuah opens in the high places and the rivers that flow from within the believer are one outpouring; the One who opens the springs IS the One who gives the living water.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27006
  FROM _s303_isa41_lookup sv, _s303_isa41_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=41 AND sv.verse_number=17
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=41 AND ev.verse_number=18
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-41-the-idols-are-nothing-wind-and-confusion',
       E'The idols are nothing — wind and confusion; Yahuah alone foretells',
       E'The court of the nations is challenged to prove their gods by foretelling: *Produce your cause, saith Yahuah (LORD)... Shew the things that are to come hereafter, that we may know that ye are gods* (Isaiah 41:21,23). They cannot, and the verdict falls: *Behold, ye are of nothing, and your work of nought: an abomination is he that chooseth you* (41:24); *Behold, they are all vanity; their works are nothing: their molten images are wind and confusion* (41:29). The whole library says the same of the idols. The psalm: *Their idols are silver and gold, the work of men''s hands. They have mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not... They that make them are like unto them* (Psalm 115:4-5,8). Jeremiah: *every founder is confounded by the graven image: for his molten image is falsehood, and there is no breath in them. They are vanity, and the work of errors: in the time of their visitation they shall perish* (Jeremiah 10:14-15). And the apostle''s plain confession: *we know that an idol is nothing in the world, and that there is none other Elohim (God) but one* (1 Corinthians 8:4). The reason the idols are nothing is sealed in the court''s own question — *Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know?* (41:26) — for Yahuah alone foretells: *I am Elohim (God), and there is none else... Declaring the end from the beginning, and from ancient times the things that are not yet done* (Isaiah 46:9-10). A thing with a carved mouth that cannot speak the latter end is wind; only the One who declares the end is Elohim.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27009
  FROM _s303_isa41_lookup sv, _s303_isa41_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=41 AND sv.verse_number=24
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=41 AND ev.verse_number=29
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

